--TEST--
An event stream is handed no peer, so its message has no frame behind it and a frame's payload is a name error rather than a `null` — `rule:concurrency/two-doors-one-isolate` and `rule:concurrency/a-connection-is-a-loop`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `Core\Socket\Message` answers four readers because two sources meet in one
// wait: a frame the peer sent, and a value the bus delivered. The other door
// takes no socket, so there is no peer and no second source -- every message
// an event stream receives is a delivery, which is why this class is `topic()`
// and `value()` and nothing else.
//
// Asking it for a frame's payload is therefore refused where it is written. A
// shared class would have answered `null` instead, which a program is free to
// read as "the peer sent nothing" rather than as "there is no peer".
class Feed {
    public static function describe(Core\Sse\Message $msg): string {
        if ($msg->value() != null) {
            return $msg->topic();
        }
        $msg->text();
        return "nothing was published";
    }
}
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0405]: `Core\Sse\Message` has no method named `text`
   --> case.nvs:16:9
   |
16 |         $msg->text();
   |         ^^^^ referenced here

error: aborting due to 1 error
